{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Liam stretched in bed, the morning sun casting familiar patterns across his walls, but something felt *off*—too clean, too symmetrical. His fingers hovered over the keyboard, and he noticed the way his reflection in the mouse glitched at the edges, like a corrupted digital frame. A sudden realization hit him: the world wasn’t *real*. He bolted upright as his bedroom tiles rearranged themselves into pixelated blocks, the air humming with a faint, synthetic white noise. Outside, the trees flickered between photorealistic and jagged polygons, their branches resetting like a buffering load screen. His stomach twisted as he stumbled to the window, only to see the street below rendered in perfect 1080p, pedestrians moving in unison like NPCs on a loop. A notification popped up in his vision, bold and glitchy: **\"CONGRATULATIONS! YOU HAVE ENTERED THE GAME MODE.\"**\n\nLiam’s hands trembled as he experimented—jumping sent him soaring through the air like a character in slow motion, walls phasing solid or dissolving at his will. He screamed, and his voice distorted into static before returning to normal. A quest log appeared in his peripheral, listing objectives like *\"Find the Hidden Glitch in Sector 7\"* and *\"Avoid the Admin.\"* Panic set in as he spotted a shadowy figure watching him from across the street, its movements too precise, its eyes two glowing red pixels. Before he could react, a familiar voice crackled over the air: *\"Welcome to your adventure, Player.\"* The words echoed like a system message, and Liam’s heart pounded as he understood—this wasn’t just a game. Someone had put him here *on purpose*.", "logprobs": [{"token": "L", "logprob": -1.2783106565475464}, {"token": "iam", "logprob": -0.04193313047289848}, {"token": " stretched", "logprob": -2.300961971282959}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -2.53041410446167}, {"token": " bed",